### 4.5 Test Data Management
#### Data Requirements
- Credential matrix: valid, expired, invalid tokens, insufficient-permission users
- Simulated 401 Unauthorized and null-description payloads

#### Data Availability
Test Type | Data Source | Environment | Data Type | Data Volume | Comments
---|---|---|---|---|---
Authentication/Authorization | Mocked Jira API | Staging | Token sets | Low | Covers valid/invalid/expired
Error Handling | Proxy/Stub | QA | Null/empty payloads | Low | Simulate inaccessible descriptions

### 4.6 Test Environments
- Integration or staging environment with controlled Jira API endpoint access
- Log/trace enabled for request/response inspection

## 7. Assumptions
- Test team has access to a Jira environment supporting 401 simulation
- Mock/stub services are available for negative path testing
- Test data can be seeded for all credential states
- No functional validation of unavailable requirements will be performed

## 3. Quality Objectives
- Validate API authentication and access permissions
- Verify error handling for missing or inaccessible Jira issue descriptions

## 4.9 Tools Table
Tool | Purpose
---|---
Playwright | UI error state validation (if applicable)
PyTest | API and backend validation
JMeter | Performance/SLA simulation for auth endpoints
OWASP ZAP | Security/negative path testing
tcconfig | Network condition simulation

## 9. Risk Mitigation Table
Risk ID | Description | Severity | Mitigation Action | Owner | Status
---|---|---|---|---|---
R1 | Dynamic database sheet connection drops during test runs | High | Use retry logic and connection pooling in test scripts | QA Lead | Open
R2 | SLA processing latency for Jira API authentication | Medium | Simulate load with JMeter, monitor response times, and alert on breaches | Performance Engineer | Open
R3 | Incomplete error logging for null/null page-load errors | High | Enhance logging and validate all error paths with negative tests | QA Lead | Open
R4 | Unavailable test data for expired/invalid tokens | Medium | Pre-seed all credential states and automate data refresh | Test Data Manager | Open
R5 | Tooling/environment access delays | Medium | Early provisioning and environment readiness checks | Project Manager | Open

## Resource & Timeline Estimate
- 1 QA Lead (test design, execution, reporting)
- 1 Automation Engineer (framework scripting, CI integration)
- 1 Test Data Manager (credential seeding, mocks)
- 1 Performance Engineer (JMeter setup, SLA validation)
- Estimated duration: 2 weeks (test design, environment prep, execution, reporting)

